{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Kei draws a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-by-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> grid. He colors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of the unit squares silver and the remaining squares gold. Kei then folds the grid in half vertically, forming pairs of overlapping unit squares. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> equal the least and greatest possible number of gold-on-gold pairs, respectively. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff842a2fca6d54b477ad6977cf9e2c632f410f90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d00727a04e32222f0e1b446a0f41cc4ef37b8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* By taesungh */ size(100);  int N = 6; int M = 3; for (int i = 0; i &lt;= N; ++i) {    draw((0,i)--(N,i));    if (i != M) {       draw((i,0)--(i,N));    } } draw((M,N+1)--(M,-1), linetype(new real[] {4,4})); [/asy]\" width=\"128\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a4a6f84c123c4ede2616a6769c48e53d6de2864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 14\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 16\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the least number of gold-on-gold pairs will be obtained when the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> silver squares are placed on the two sides so that they don't overlap when folded over (because then it will minimize the number of gold-on-golds). We can see that if we split them up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides, and then fold it, the number of gold-on-golds will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed8d26c0c49a0543c7c46566853b83d821c90332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18-13 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The maximum number of gold-on-golds will be achieved when the silver squares overlap when folded over, which will increase the number of gold-on-golds. If we align 6 silver squares with each other on each side, and put the last one somewhere else, we get the maximum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f058942e6976ba2c671a98177a17f3a79d0ae2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 - 7 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/35449ac1ab280374321f1a610bf749c3ac345d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11+5=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~Sigmacuber\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=ixE4Cgx2jsbHnQNW&amp;t=4025\">https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=ixE4Cgx2jsbHnQNW&amp;t=4025</a>\n~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jTTcscvcQmI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jTTcscvcQmI</a>\nYou can contact him through his Youtube Channel\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick.2C_fast.2C_easy.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\">Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fdG7EDW_7xk\">https://youtu.be/fdG7EDW_7xk</a> \n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=WhpkSTD3UJpbQ3KC&amp;t=1572\">https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=WhpkSTD3UJpbQ3KC&amp;t=1572</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988\">https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=1344s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=1344s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1JvuP6ME13/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1JvuP6ME13/?spm_id_from=333.1387